Third-party
-----------

The ideas loam builds on are prior art: sparse volumetric grids,
octree acceleration structures, persistent (copy-on-write) trees,
explicit finite-difference operators and L-system-style growth are
well-published territory. The design and the Zig implementation in this
repo are original. loam depends on the sibling common and struple
libraries, each of which carries its own (identical, dual) license in
its own repository.

The Apache 2.0 license file applies to all source code and
documentation in this repository (`src/`, `py/`, `tools/`, `docs/`,
`build.zig`, `build.zig.zon`, `README.md`). It does not extend to
scenes, fields or grown structures that hosts feed through or draw out
of a mounted loam at runtime — those belong to their authors.
